# Binary assets git must never line-ending-normalise.
#
# reportlab's PDF output contains few NUL bytes near the top of the file, so
# git's text/binary heuristic misread bp-central-blood-pressure-log.pdf as
# text and rewrote LF to CRLF on checkout: 7112 bytes stored, 7211 bytes on
# disk, 99 injected bytes. Viewers are lenient enough to still open it, which
# is exactly what makes the failure easy to miss - every byte offset in the
# xref table is silently wrong.
#
# PNGs were never affected because they carry NUL bytes early. Declaring the
# whole family is cheaper than waiting to find out which format trips the
# heuristic next.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
